1
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,840
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa

2
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too

3
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:42,260
onto the head of the
carpenter I had in a choke hold

4
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:48,440
They laughed that I'm still just a brat

5
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if you lose your spirit,
Katsushika is there for you

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,600
Even a single yawn doesn't change

7
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,540
The streetscape feels strangely gentle

8
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:10,460
From the water tower with the pointed hat

9
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:16,780
the sun sets over the rented shops

10
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end just like this, too

11
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
happiness again, they say

12
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,760
I only realized it after losing it

13
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,940
Because I'm such a fool

14
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:41,140
Ryo-san will become a manga artist

15
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:46,880
Wow, Honba-san

16
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,200
What's wrong with you?

17
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:52,040
What happened, Honda?

18
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:00,420
Even though the results
were riding on it too

19
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:03,860
Hey, Honda! Thanks to you,
all my hard work was for nothing

20
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:37,000
Wasn't she the hugely popular shoujo
manga artist under the pen name Ai no Miko?

21
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,880
We all understand already,
you don't need to explain it so thoroughly.

22
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:43,260
So, what's going on with Nana Otohime?

23
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:47,320
She hasn't met me since the other day,
and she won't answer my calls either.

24
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:52,140
Honda, go ahead and cry
your heart out on my chest!

25
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:52,860
Cramped.

26
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,640
It's all over. Give up.

27
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:56,240
No way...

28
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,960
Ryo-chan, it's too cruel to
jump to conclusions like that.

29
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,160
That's right.

30
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:09,340
Probably because she has a new boyfriend, you know.
Don't cry. How were things between you two lately?

31
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:18,380
Do you have any idea why? The last time we met was two weeks ago.
Did you do something to make her hate you then?

32
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:25,440
No, nothing like that. It was a normal date.
Come on, did you at least kiss her, or did you just work the whole time?

33
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,640
Ryo-chan

34
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:28,580
I wouldn't do anything like that.

35
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:32,720
First, we went to see a movie.

36
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:37,100
After that, we rode our bike
across the Tokyo Bay Aqua-Line.

37
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:40,900
On the way, we stopped at Umi
Hotaru and had soft serve ice cream.

38
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,220
On the way back,
we had dinner at a family restaurant.

39
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:46,800
I took her all the way
to her apartment building.

40
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,720
There's nothing about that that would make her hate you,
is there?

41
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,380
If anything, we're a lovey-dovey couple.

42
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:57,120
Maybe there's some other reason,
isn't there?

43
00:03:57,560 --> 00:04:00,859
Right, what was the name
of Otohime's editor again?

44
00:04:00,909 --> 00:04:01,840
That editor.

45
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:03,960
Was it Ryusenshi Hyō-san?

46
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:07,020
That's the one. Let's ask him.

47
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:11,020
Here it is, here it is.

48
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:13,460
Yo, make a copy of this.

49
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:16,700
Well, they probably say that to everyone,
don't they?

50
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,180
Well, you really do have the will to write,
don't you.

51
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:18,840
Yeah.

52
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,480
Well then, that's settled.

53
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,000
And who are you two?

54
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,440
Actually, Miko is in a slump right now.

55
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:31,500
She's having trouble finding the direction
for her new series, which was supposed to kick off with a big crossover.

56
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,140
That's why she won't even pick up the phone.

57
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:35,820
So that means...

58
00:04:35,820 --> 00:04:39,580
Good for you, Honda!
Looks like she hasn't dumped you yet!

59
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:40,280
Yes.

60
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,760
That's not good at all.

61
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:44,600
Miko is at a crucial point in her
career as a manga artist right now.

62
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:47,860
If things go on like this,
who knows what will become of her future.

63
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:51,200
This is a crucial time
for shoujo manga artists.

64
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:54,860
We editors have to be very careful too.

65
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:56,320
Like she got dumped by her boyfriend,

66
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,140
or her bed caught a cold,

67
00:04:58,140 --> 00:04:59,640
or she got a new boyfriend.

68
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:03,400
Her state of mind directly affects her work.

69
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:06,320
I see, being an editor is tough too.

70
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:09,240
Speaking of editors, the people here

71
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:12,700
are all like they jumped
straight out of a shoujo manga.

72
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:15,940
This is a shoujo manga editorial department,
after all.

73
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:19,680
The shonen manga editorial
departments are completely different.

74
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:26,380
This is a photo from when I was at Young Dandy,
working on Otoko no Hanamichi.

75
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:30,500
It was taken with Jimmy Takenaka-sensei,
a former biker gang member turned author.

76
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,360
Sounds like they were in the same gang

77
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:34,560
What's his name?

78
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,000
How do you read it?

79
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:37,320
Bari-bari?

80
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,620
It's written "Ogon,
" but you read it as "Kin."

81
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:41,260
It's Bari-bari King.

82
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:41,960
I see.

83
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:44,740
And this one is from
when I was at Eros Heaven.

84
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:48,180
This is a photo and business card
from Ogeretsu Erokichi-sensei.

85
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:51,140
What? I'm a huge fan of Ogeretsu Erokichi!

86
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,400
It's that perverted style that's so good.

87
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:55,000
What does he look like?

88
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:58,300
He's as much of a pervert as in the manga

89
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,240
But to match it this closely...

90
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,300
Your name?

91
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:03,300
That's easy enough to understand.

92
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:05,000
Ignorant Shibakuro?

93
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,460
And this is Ryusenshi Hyō,
the editor in charge of Ai no Miko.

94
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,880
I've been working with her since she
debuted in her third year of junior high.

95
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:15,220
So you've known her far longer than Honda

96
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:20,400
No wonder so many editors end
up marrying shoujo manga artists.

97
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:23,840
Don't say such nasty things, senpai.

98
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:26,740
There's no need to worry about that.

99
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,880
Miko is devoted to Honda and no one else.

100
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:32,200
Ever since Honda confessed to her,
her name drafts have been coming in faster.

101
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,880
The heroine has also
started to feel more dynamic.

102
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,200
That's Yataka?

103
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,400
No, that's not...

104
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:41,280
So I'd like you both to help
Miko recover from her slump.

105
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:42,880
We'd really appreciate your cooperation.

106
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:46,860
Please. If it doesn't get to the printers today,
we're really in trouble.

107
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:52,680
No good! I can't draw it!

108
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:56,360
That's not true. It'll be fine, really.

109
00:06:56,410 --> 00:06:59,340
Hey, hey, Nana, don't cry.

110
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:02,140
What on earth are you trying to draw?

111
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:05,631
This time, to open up new
possibilities for shoujo manga,

112
00:07:05,681 --> 00:07:08,540
I'm making the theme a
friendship between men.

113
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:11,220
A friendship between men?

114
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:18,340
I just can't draw the fight scene where men
punch each other to confirm their friendship.

115
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:21,000
Is that all it is?

116
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:24,940
Ryo-san, could you help me?

117
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:26,600
Leave it to me.

118
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:32,320
How's that?

119
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,060
Go easier on me.

120
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:38,340
Between men, friendship doesn't
need any holding back, does it, Miko?

121
00:07:38,340 --> 00:07:41,479
Yeah, but still, not just punching,

122
00:07:41,529 --> 00:07:43,040
like heel drops or something.

123
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:45,780
I see, heel drops. Okay.

124
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:50,040
How about this? Like this?

125
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:52,460
No, that's wrong. Maybe a reverse crab hold?

126
00:07:54,460 --> 00:07:55,640
I give up! I give up! I give up!

127
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:56,640
How was that?

128
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:59,680
I think it should be a
choke-slipper after all.

129
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:02,040
Manji hold.

130
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,540
Suplex.

131
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,240
Elbow drop.

132
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:06,620
Tate-ami hankī.

133
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:08,560
Giant swing!

134
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:10,680
then head straight for the window,

135
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,980
and throw her!

136
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:16,940
Whoa, that was close.

137
00:08:16,990 --> 00:08:19,880
Hey, this is a misunderstanding!

138
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:20,760
What are you doing!

139
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:21,880
Miko, how was it?

140
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,420
Maybe it's better if you fall after all.

141
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,040
Idiot, don't come over!

142
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:31,060
Don't worry. With your stamina,
a height like this is no problem.

143
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:32,920
What are you talking about!

144
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:36,620
What kind of calculation gets
you to the answer that it's fine!

145
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:39,460
Falling really is too much of a stretch,
after all.

146
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:46,540
I fell by myself.

147
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:49,060
Hey, help me.

148
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,880
I see, so that's how you writhe around.

149
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:55,680
This really is useful for reference,
isn't it.

150
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:59,800
When Nana gets absorbed into her work,
she doesn't see what's going on around her.

151
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:02,780
Damn, nobody came to help after all.

152
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:05,180
See, I knew it would be fine.

153
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:07,740
Please don't copy this, everyone.

154
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:10,180
You were saved because it's Senpai Ryotsu,
you know.

155
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:13,220
I'm not immortal, you know.

156
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:15,000
Senpai, are you all right?

157
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,660
Of course I'm not all right.

158
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,520
Drawing manga is this hard, you know.

159
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,960
What is it this time?

160
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:28,680
I can't write the scene where two
men hug to confirm their friendship.

161
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,860
Since when is that kind
of friendship a thing?

162
00:09:31,120 --> 00:09:33,800
It's a sign of beautiful
friendship between men.

163
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,880
It's absolutely, absolutely necessary.

164
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:37,980
Don't cry, Miko.

165
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:41,300
Well, there are two men right here.
Go ahead and do it.

166
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,440
That's right.

167
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:44,780
What a stupid thing to say, you two!

168
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:46,320
Senpai, let's do it.

169
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:47,460
Calm down, Honda.

170
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:49,960
Do you want Miko's career
as a manga artist to end?

171
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:51,360
This is your fault.

172
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:53,340
W-what? No, Senpai!

173
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:55,620
No, stop it! Don't! Stop!

174
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:58,560
Hands on your hips,
lean your cheek in closer.

175
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:00,100
Smile!

176
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,500
Perfect!

177
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,160
What now, Miko?

178
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:08,320
In police uniforms, I can't get the image.

179
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,020
What did you say?

180
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:12,200
Senpai, it's for Nana-chan. Let's do it.

181
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,360
Hey, stop it.

182
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:13,940
Yaaah!

183
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:15,740
Senpai, stop!

184
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:18,240
You bastard,
you're the one who said we should do it!

185
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,480
Now that it's come to this,
we just have to go for it!

186
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:24,540
Aaaah, this just isn't going to work!

187
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:33,780
No talent? That's not true. The model was just too ugly. Hey, I'm not joking!
You didn't pick this line of work because you like it, you bastard.

188
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:41,000
It's not Miko's fault.
Sorry, I just stepped out for a drink.

189
00:10:42,020 --> 00:10:45,360
I told you,
shoujo manga artists are delicate.

190
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:50,060
What do we do? We're out of time,
and there'll be a hole in the manuscript!

191
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:51,280
It's not our fault!

192
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:56,120
Oh no, what do we do?
We can't ask anyone else at this point.

193
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:04,100
Senpai, we're being chased by time!

194
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:06,160
We can't make excuses with this.

195
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,240
Hey, how many pages is that manuscript?

196
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,180
It's thirty pages.

197
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:17,600
Thirty pages? If it were me, I could draw them in thirty minutes.
One page a minute! Really?

198
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:24,020
Senpai, you're quick at everything. If that's really true,
then just draw those thirty pages, whatever it takes!

199
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:32,280
Right now! But in return, I'm taking my full manuscript fee.
Alright, bring me the goddess and the ink!

200
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:38,740
Yes! Drawing on the stairs? That's the same as the rough draft,
pen up and...

201
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:40,440
Alright, it's done!

202
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:41,320
This is...

203
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:44,800
A masterpiece, right?

204
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:47,460
Senpai,
you really do have a talent for manga.

205
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:49,560
It's terrible.

206
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:53,560
But because of that,
readers might think it's a dream.

207
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:55,880
Alright, let's go with this.

208
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:56,720
Yay!

209
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:59,420
With this, I'm making my manga debut too!

210
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,880
Ta-da! Robo Dekaban!

211
00:12:14,060 --> 00:12:16,100
Saku, Ryozu, Patricia, Kanko

212
00:12:16,540 --> 00:12:18,420
Hey, there's a big Buddha statue nearby.

213
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:20,720
Let's buy it for 10 billion yen.

214
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,000
Tsk tsk, hey you, bro, hold on a second.

215
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,820
Robo Dekaban!

216
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,420
It's over now, Robo Dekaban appears!

217
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:27,960
Beep beep beep!

218
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:28,720
What?

219
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,600
Go, Robo Dekaban!

220
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:31,580
Roar!

221
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:33,580
What, it's tiny, aru.

222
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:34,860
I'm not scared of something like this.

223
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:37,020
Crunch! Gyafun!

224
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:48,220
Is this what you call shōjo manga, that Robo Dekaban you drew?
That's the selling point. Shōjo manga is all big eyes with little stars sparkling in them.

225
00:12:48,220 --> 00:12:58,980
So this wild, rugged style looks fresh at a glance.
To me, it doesn't look wild or rugged so much as like you just slapped it down without any effort.

226
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:04,100
To me, it just looks like a clumsy, messy drawing.
Those who know how to look will see its appeal.

227
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:07,840
Is that so?
There are ink smudges all over the place.

228
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:12,040
After all, we drew it in thirty minutes.
There was no time for corrections.

229
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:14,720
But doesn't that handmade
feel make it better?

230
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:16,940
Ryo-sensei.

231
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:18,720
What is it?

232
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,640
Ryo-sensei, we did it.

233
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,240
Sensei?

234
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:25,480
That manga placed third in the reader poll.

235
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,740
What? Really?

236
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,000
Well, it's only natural.

237
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,520
I never expected this kind of result.

238
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:34,400
I can't believe a manga
like this did so well.

239
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:37,840
Our magazine was short on gags,
so readers went wild for it.

240
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:40,000
Please,
we'd love for you to continue next week too.

241
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:43,920
Believe it or not, I'm pretty busy myself.

242
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,400
Please, make an exception for us.

243
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,160
Wait a moment.

244
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:51,820
My schedule's been
packed for the last month.

245
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,140
Please, we'll pay you double.

246
00:13:55,140 --> 00:13:58,260
Well, I don't really
care about the pay, but -

247
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:02,260
As a public servant, it's my duty
to help ordinary folks in trouble.

248
00:14:02,260 --> 00:14:03,020
Alright, I'll draw it.

249
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:04,000
Thank you so much.

250
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:07,400
Then I'll go report to the
editor-in-chief right away.

251
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:10,740
Don't forget to bring a
gift next time you come.

252
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:11,880
Understood.

253
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,780
That's amazing, Ryo-san!

254
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:18,620
Just like that,
you're a popular manga artist now.

255
00:14:18,620 --> 00:14:21,720
Well, of course.
Given my talent, it's only natural.

256
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,460
Once your comics start coming out,

257
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:25,360
you'll be rich from royalties!

258
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:26,360
Comics?

259
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:28,060
That means the collected volumes, you know.

260
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:31,440
Some comics these days have a
first printing of a million copies.

261
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:35,260
If it sold a million copies,
how much would the royalties be?

262
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:39,440
Let's see, if one volume is 390 yen,

263
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:42,400
and the royalty rate is about 10%,

264
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,960
that's roughly 39 million yen.

265
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:49,480
39 million yen!? From just one volume?

266
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:50,484
Yes,

267
00:14:50,534 --> 00:14:54,480
of course, that's if it becomes a
popular manga that everyone in Japan knows.

268
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:56,475
Alright! Let's go to the
editorial office right away and

269
00:14:56,525 --> 00:14:59,120
get them to print a
million copies of the comics!

270
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:02,680
Senpai!

271
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,700
She's gone.

272
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:10,220
Once she's like that, she won't
listen even if you try to stop her.

273
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:14,800
Honda. You've been awfully
quiet this whole time.

274
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:15,900
Well...

275
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:16,980
Here it is, right here.

276
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:20,440
What? Nana's taking a break?

277
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:21,920
Nana...

278
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:24,640
What?

279
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,110
Adding a special one-shot,

280
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,880
they want a million-copy
comic collection right away?

281
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:33,420
Yeah, with the remaining pages,
I can finish it in about three days.

282
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:34,840
Don't be ridiculous.

283
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:37,440
No rookie can suddenly
sell a million copies.

284
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,860
But my manga placed third
in the popularity poll!

285
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:42,740
It's a sure thing it'll sell.

286
00:15:42,740 --> 00:15:45,620
I think it was just a novelty, though.

287
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:46,860
That's not true.

288
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:48,440
Next time it's third to second,

289
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:51,580
and after that it'll surely
take the unshakable first place.

290
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:54,160
Don't joke like that.

291
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:56,320
This world isn't that easy, you know.

292
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:56,920
What?

293
00:15:57,180 --> 00:15:59,560
I've been in this business for 25 years,

294
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:01,341
and from what I've seen,

295
00:16:01,391 --> 00:16:04,140
this manga's popularity will
drop sharply starting next time.

296
00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:07,600
Then what if it takes first place next time?

297
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:09,640
No way that could ever happen.

298
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:10,400
Hahaha.

299
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:15,320
Then if it does take first place, you'll publish
a million copies of my comic collection, right?

300
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:18,520
Fine. Go ahead and try, if you can.

301
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:19,180
Hahaha.

302
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:20,760
This guy's joking way too much.

303
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:23,220
Alright, it's a promise. Got it?

304
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,760
Ryusei, come here for a moment.

305
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:25,440
Hmph.

306
00:16:26,180 --> 00:16:28,540
How do they actually conduct
these popularity polls?

307
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,140
It's the reader survey postcard, you know.

308
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:34,300
On the survey postcards
included in the magazine,

309
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,860
readers write down their
favorite manga and manga artists,

310
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:41,840
and tens of thousands of postcards sent in from
across the country are tallied up to gather data,

311
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:44,440
and that's how they produce the popularity
ranking for each work every time.

312
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:48,000
Since they use these rankings to
decide whether a series gets cancelled,

313
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,900
it's pretty much the same as TV ratings.

314
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:53,960
I see, so numbers really are power.

315
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:56,580
Just you watch.

316
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,160
Right.

317
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:03,540
I came to the editorial office. I'm
going to draw next week's manuscript here.

318
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:08,000
Let's see... Okay, this'll do.

319
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:10,060
I'm borrowing a pen.

320
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,860
Alright, I'm on a roll!

321
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:15,140
W-what a man.

322
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:28,660
P-please, just spare my life.

323
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:32,200
Is Weekly Sapphire in there?

324
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:33,920
I'll take all of it.

325
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:36,180
But you'll be paid on credit, got it?

326
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:36,820
Understood?

327
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:39,160
T-thank you very much.

328
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:43,420
Welcome.

329
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:45,440
Do you have Weekly Sapphire?

330
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:48,080
I'll take all of it.

331
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:48,640
Y-yes.

332
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,660
Hey, hey!

333
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:04,720
Hurry up, Shogun!

334
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:07,880
The more you do,
the more your workload goes up!

335
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:08,740
Keep it up!

336
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:12,120
But Ryotsu,
are you really sure this will be okay?

337
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:13,640
Don't worry.

338
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:15,220
If the comic collection
sells a million copies,

339
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:17,620
royalties come in even if it doesn't sell.

340
00:18:17,980 --> 00:18:18,600
Really?

341
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,420
Yeah, so just relax like you're on a big ship,
alright?

342
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:21,920
Yeah.

343
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:25,680
This means first place
in the poll is guaranteed!

344
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:29,180
W-what? Robo Dekaban Banchou
is number one in popularity?

345
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,920
I-I can't believe it.

346
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:33,040
It's gathering overwhelming support.

347
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:36,420
Nonsense,
are all our readers complete idiots?

348
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:40,040
How rude,
it just means my manga is a masterpiece.

349
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:41,760
Do you have this week's issue?

350
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:42,260
Yes.

351
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:45,080
This thing is ranked first?

352
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:48,440
How can you say such a thing
about the first-place work?

353
00:18:48,440 --> 00:18:51,020
S-sorry, that just slipped out.
My true feelings.

354
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:54,240
As promised, you're publishing
a million copies right now.

355
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:59,360
But a million copies of this...
where's your common sense as an editor?

356
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:01,480
A promise is a promise, isn't it?

357
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:02,280
F-fine, I understand.

358
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:05,080
A million comic volumes?

359
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:05,860
That's right!

360
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:08,520
Ryo-san, we did it! Now we're rich!

361
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:11,240
The 39 million yen in royalties is ours!

362
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:18,200
Look at me, coming back here again.

363
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:23,820
I went and bought Nana's favorite cake,
didn't I.

364
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:26,980
Nana-chan.

365
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:29,380
Honda-san.

366
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:30,760
Where is everyone?

367
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:32,240
We sent them home.

368
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:34,460
Because there's no way to get
any work done with them here.

369
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:36,380
I see... but I brought cake for nothing.

370
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:37,000
Honda-san.

371
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,380
What's wrong with Nana-chan?

372
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,220
But I just can't come up
with ideas for a new series.

373
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:44,620
Nana-chan.

374
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:48,780
Nana-chan,
have you been riding a motorcycle lately?

375
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:53,660
Let's go for a ride to clear
our heads once in a while.

376
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,220
I'll come along too.

377
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:56,320
Honda-san.

378
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:03,460
A biker mustn't be troubled by worries,
you know.

379
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:06,760
Aaaaaah!

380
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:08,880
Aaaaaah!

381
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,940
Here comes the name of Pure Bushy!

382
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:18,060
Eeeeeeh!

383
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:30,980
That feels good.

384
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,760
It feels like I've been
freed after such a long time.

385
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:35,020
Good.

386
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:40,480
You're completely different, Honda, when
you're riding a bike and when you're not.

387
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:42,460
Yeah, I hear that a lot.

388
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:48,500
But you also look different, Nana, when
you're frowning and thinking about manga.

389
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:52,380
Really? I guess it's because I love bikes.

390
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:56,180
So, Nana, how did you come to love bikes?

391
00:20:56,540 --> 00:21:00,600
Me? It was when I was in my
first year of high school.

392
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:05,800
On my way to the editorial office with my manuscript,
I suddenly felt sick.

393
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:11,640
A rider happened to pass by
and took me to the hospital.

394
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:14,605
That rider,

395
00:21:14,655 --> 00:21:18,680
to me, was like a prince on a white horse.

396
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:21,680
I think I had a similar experience...

397
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:23,217
That rider,

398
00:21:23,267 --> 00:21:26,600
didn't he have a kill mark
or something on his helmet?

399
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,840
Now that you mention it...

400
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:32,740
I was following you!

401
00:21:33,140 --> 00:21:37,360
The place was in front of a vending machine
just off the Tamagawa riverside in Kawasaki.

402
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,820
How do you know that?

403
00:21:38,980 --> 00:21:40,760
Well, why do you ask...

404
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:44,080
Honda-san?

405
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:49,460
Well, back in the day
I was a hardcore rider.

406
00:21:49,460 --> 00:21:52,260
Still, I never expected it would be you,
Nana-chan.

407
00:21:52,260 --> 00:21:57,280
So Honda-san and I were fated to meet,
as if the gods had planned it.

408
00:21:57,280 --> 00:21:58,080
Surely.

409
00:21:58,080 --> 00:21:59,840
Yeah, the motorcycles are
also thanks to the gods, right?

410
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:01,300
Haha.

411
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:06,220
Hey Nana-chan, how about changing the world of
motorcycles you love at the New Year's festival?

412
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:07,720
The world of motorcycles?

413
00:22:08,100 --> 00:22:08,380
Yeah.

414
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:11,580
The world of motorcycles.

415
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:14,800
Thank you, Honda-san.

416
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:17,440
With that,
I feel like I could somehow draw it.

417
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,980
I'm really glad.

418
00:22:19,380 --> 00:22:22,540
I'm a huge fan of Ai no Miko-chan's manga,
after all.

419
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:27,480
This is Nana's new series.

420
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:29,520
So she finally came up with an idea.

421
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,700
Thanks to you two.

422
00:22:30,700 --> 00:22:34,560
Having Shirobai appear in
a shoujo manga is so fresh.

423
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:37,000
With this, it's sure to be a hit.

424
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,140
Too naive, too naive.

425
00:22:38,380 --> 00:22:42,200
Compared to my number one popularity hit,
Robo Dekaban, it's still nowhere near.

426
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:46,600
Orai orai orai orai orai

427
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:47,300
Alright, stop!

428
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:48,300
Alright, Sensei.

429
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:50,100
Hey, was it you?

430
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:54,900
Not a single copy of this book sold,
so all one million copies were returned.

431
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:56,160
What?!

432
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:57,040
Okay.

433
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:01,200
Whoa, stop it!

434
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:14,860
Ryo-san, what are we going to do?

435
00:23:15,340 --> 00:23:18,160
Once it's published,
the royalties are all mine.

436
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:18,960
Ryo...

437
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:21,380
The cost of the manga we bought on credit,

438
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:22,820
which we covered for you,

439
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:25,240
and the postage for the postcards.
You'll pay us back.

440
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:26,340
I know.

441
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:27,160
How much is it?

442
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,160
The 300,000 manga copies
we bought up come to

443
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:30,280
75 million yen.

444
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:33,680
Stamps at 50 yen each,
300,000 of them, is 15 million yen.

445
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:37,520
And the part-timers we hired cost 5 million.

446
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:40,240
That's 95 million yen in total.

447
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:43,600
So after subtracting,
we're left with a 56 million yen deficit.

448
00:23:44,020 --> 00:23:45,520
56 million.

449
00:23:48,660 --> 00:23:50,060
Hey, don't run away!

450
00:23:50,060 --> 00:23:51,960
I just remembered something I had to do.

451
00:23:56,960 --> 00:24:00,180
Forget it! Living is a real grind!

452
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:20,080
Even at midnight, a call comes in...

453
00:24:20,080 --> 00:24:27,300
If it's you, waking up feels good.

454
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:36,520
Even boring talk warms up your whole body.

455
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:43,140
But I want to see my friends.

456
00:24:43,140 --> 00:24:46,980
I just want to be loved, surely.

457
00:24:47,600 --> 00:24:52,600
Just enough to make everyone tease.

458
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:35,200
Next time: Fierce battle!
The Great Kick-the-Can War!

459
00:25:36,020 --> 00:25:37,600
Ryōzai, gepō kopen

